	shape: "octagon",
	description: "How to see recipes and how to inspect blocks",
	text: [
		"I'll give you a few tips about how to use JEI and WAILA, these are important mods that you'll use. If you know how, go to the next quest.",
		"",
		"Just Enough Items (JEI) is a mod that adds a catalog of items with their recipes and uses:",
		"",
		"- The item catalog can be toggled by pressing 'CTRL + O' while your inventory is opened.",
		"",
		"- You may bookmark items and liquids by pressing \"A\" while hovering them, these will appear at the left of your inventory, press \"A\" while hovering the item again to remove it.",
		"",
		"- Pressing R on an item in your inventory will show you it's recipes, pressing U on an item will show you it's uses.",
		"",
		"- When browsing recipes, if you have minimal perception skills you will see several arrows pointing to the left and right, these give you more recipes if you click them. You will also see that there are other crafting stations that look odd and complicated, these are machines, most of which you will get and use later so don't worry.",
		"",
		"",
		"WAILA (What Am I Looking At?) is a mod that gives you information about the block you are looking at at the top of your screen:",
		"",
		"- This may be configured to show even more information, but you don't need that much.",
		"",
		"- It will show blocks, liquids and entities.",
		"",
		"- The information is displayed on top of your screen."
	],
